# What ran before a step in an arm is what ran before its choice and what ran before it in its own arm (#329): the
# shelf is set up in the arm that keeps anything, and the report is kept in an arm of a choice inside that arm. A choice
# inside an arm is a branch of the arm's choice that runs when every arm on its path holds (`KEEP · REPORT`), so both
# calls stand in `main/?1`, on two branches that are not apart: the set-up stands before the report in the arm both are
# in. It ran before `keep_report`, and `write` under it writes the report in `out`, the folder the set-up decides.

route arms.main
choice main/?1
step main/?1/open_shelf
step main/?1/open_shelf/Shelf()
step main/?1/Shelf.keep_report
step main/?1/Shelf.keep_report/write

line entry > main call
line main/?1/open_shelf/Shelf() > Shelf@main/?1/open_shelf/Shelf() value
line Shelf@main/?1/open_shelf/Shelf() > main/?1/open_shelf value
line main/?1/open_shelf > Shelf·shelf@main/?1/open_shelf value
line Shelf·shelf@main/?1/open_shelf > main/?1/Shelf.keep_report/write value     # `write(self.root / "report.txt", text)`
line main/?1/Shelf.keep_report/write > File(out/report.txt) own

home Shelf@main/?1/open_shelf/Shelf() main/?1/open_shelf
home Shelf·shelf@main/?1/open_shelf main/?1

side entry left
side File(out/report.txt) right
